rationale: Hypothesis: integer indexing gathers only the selected embedding rows, avoiding a 4096×8192 one-hot tensor and its large matrix multiplication. The per-row solve by a diagonal matrix is equivalent to dividing centered rows by their spread, and vmap replaces the sequential map with a batched transform that XLA can schedule across the GPU. Expected HLO/profile: replace one-hot plus large dot with gather; remove diagonal construction and solve; expose batched projection operations instead of a map loop. Risk: batched execution may change floating-point accumulation slightly, and the rewrite must still match the reference within its rtol/atol. When timing asynchronously dispatched JAX work, call block_until_ready before recording elapsed time.
