rationale: The reference constructs a dense 8192×8192 band matrix and uses matrix products, although each output position only needs values from at most 33 nearby positions. A 1D convolution computes local sums and squared sums with 33 taps, avoiding the huge intermediate and dense products. The maximum absolute standardized value is the same as the last element of the sorted absolute values, so it can be computed with a reduction.
